"from": 230,
"to": 240,
"text": "The gates run on this Windows host during /implement. The chunk adds a product crate and changes the root manifest, so the supply-chain gates run: `cargo deny check`, the new sole-root tokio ban for `viola-channel` and the ban probes. The integration suite runs with `AGENT_RUN_KEEP_HOMES=1` so the G4 schema-check and the secret scan read the new homes. A boot smoke is listed because `src/cmd/run.rs` is the boot path: a mint-then-read session `p-channel-smoke` with an idempotent pre-clean; its `boot` readiness now includes the snapshot `endpoint` (step 14) and its `cleanup` reports `endpoint_gone:true`. The `pre-push` entry is the mutation and coverage gate: the Linux suites and `ubuntu-latest` leg in WSL, the new `windows-tests` coverage stage and the `windows-2025` leg here, and CI's union — the diff carries `#[cfg(unix)]` bodies (verification-harness.md 2026-09-25). Stop rust-analyzer by exact `ExecutablePath` before it (host-win32.md 2026-09-26). The fuzz target is exercised by CI's `fuzz-replay` job (Linux only), read through the CI entry. CI reads: a check that completes failed ends the read red at once; a green read waits for the run to complete (overseer directive 2026-09-27, item 1)."
}
],
